1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,882
Keeping a Useful Project Log Our project log stated that work was

2
00:00:04,895 --> 00:00:12,066
currently behind schedule Hitherto the team had relied on informal updates Henceforth

3
00:00:12,237 --> 00:00:17,408
each member would record progress weekly The first review identified a delay

4
00:00:17,605 --> 00:00:25,118
subsequently we revised the timetable Thereafter reports became more consistent The log

5
00:00:25,132 --> 00:00:30,158
was useful because it explained decisions not just dates A note might

6
00:00:30,171 --> 00:00:32,960
say that a change could pose a risk or that a resource

7
00:00:32,974 --> 00:00:36,829
was on the verge of running out Another would explain why an

8
00:00:36,842 --> 00:00:41,539
apparently easy solution had proved of no avail A summary referred to

9
00:00:41,553 --> 00:00:47,421
a problem and the lessons contained therein Formal connectors should clarify relationships

10
00:00:47,526 --> 00:00:53,039
not decorate a paragraph Incidentally an extra fact belongs only where it

11
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:58,224
helps the reader A record becomes confusing when every sentence sounds official

12
00:00:58,237 --> 00:01:02,487
but no one can tell what happened The best account lets readers

13
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,237
trace a decision understand its reason and see what followed
